abstract: >-
  A comprehensive, publication-grade clinical machine learning framework evaluating deep tabular
  architectures (HeartMLP, TabTransformer), patient-similarity Graph Neural Networks (GCN, GAT),
  and gradient-boosted baselines across multi-center cardiovascular disease cohorts (Cleveland,
  Hungarian, Switzerland, VA Long Beach) and MIMIC-IV ICU hospital mortality. Integrates post-hoc
  Temperature Scaling, Deep Ensembles, Split and Mondrian Conformal Prediction for finite-sample
  coverage guarantees under domain shift, Doubly Robust Causal Inference (IPTW/AIPW with sensitivity
  E-values), Equal Opportunity demographic fairness calibration, and closed-loop actionable
  counterfactual recourse.
